cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code or data, please cite it as below. The associated
  manuscript has not yet been published; once it is, please cite the article.
type: software
title: >-
  Same Rivers, Different Priorities: How Environmental Maps Shape
  Conservation Decisions — reproducibility code and data
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, derived data and figure/table scripts for a national-scale
  study of how the choice of land-cover representation (CORINE Land Cover
  2018 and Living England Phase IV, native and grain-controlled) changes
  fixed-budget river-survey prioritisation for a forage-oriented Eurasian
  beaver indicator across 76,082 eligible river reaches in 105 English
  catchments.
